// Expected: a0 at one session and at two.
//
// session_sign_oracle_cross.vp with a scenarios block that binds a public
// label Bob never uses in the signature. Routing Alice's challenge to Bob's
// other run and bringing its answer back forges nothing, and the label the
// scenario rebinds appears nowhere in what Alice accepts.
//
// The engine used to withdraw the matching-run exemption anyway. Two clones
// of a principal are interchangeable only where the scenario left that
// principal's bindings alone, and the comparison was over the whole binding
// set, so any binding at all made every clone of Bob a different run and the
// signature he genuinely produced was reported as the attacker's. The
// question is now asked per value: a binding separates two clones only where
// the value in hand depends on something the scenario rebinds, which is what
// keeps `spore_ns_pk.vp` at `a1` — Lowe's `m1` is sealed to the bound peer
// key itself.

attacker[active]

principal Alice[
	knows public label_one, label_two, label
	generates na
]

principal Bob[
	knows private sk
	knows public label_one, label_two, label
	pk = PUBKEY(sk)
	generates nb
	_ = HASH(label)
]

Bob -> Alice: [pk], nb

Alice -> Bob: na

principal Bob[
	sig = SIGN(sk, CONCAT(na, nb))
]

Bob -> Alice: sig

principal Alice[
	_ = SIGNVERIF(pk, CONCAT(na, nb), sig)?
]

scenarios[
	Bob[label = label_one]
	Bob[label = label_two]
]

queries[
	authentication? Bob -> Alice: sig
]
